From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessio Corsi <alessio.corsi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:02:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sunxi: a733: clock the card from the oscillator in a
 blob-less SPL

The MMC driver takes clocks above 24 MHz from PLL_PERIPH0 as it finds
it. On the A733 nothing in U-Boot sets that PLL up, and an SPL built with
SUNXI_A733_DRAM_SOURCE runs no blob that might have.

Use the 24 MHz oscillator for every card clock in such an SPL, as the
manufacturer's loader does. The card then runs at 24 MHz at most while
the SPL loads U-Boot.
---
 drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c
index a65747e7..a994801d 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c
@@ -56,6 +56,18 @@ static bool sunxi_mmc_a733_spl(void)
 	       IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MACH_SUN60I_A733);
 }
 
+/*
+ * An A733 SPL that initialises DRAM itself runs without the libdram blob
+ * and on the clocks the boot ROM left: nothing has set up PLL_PERIPH0.
+ * Clock the card from the 24 MHz oscillator, as the manufacturer's loader
+ * does; that caps it at 24 MHz, which is enough to load U-Boot.
+ */
+static bool sunxi_mmc_osc_only(void)
+{
+	return sunxi_mmc_a733_spl() &&
+	       IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SUNXI_A733_DRAM_SOURCE);
+}
+
 /*
  * Keep A733 SPL controller programming stages apart. Without these gaps,
  * back-to-back operations become unreliable; serial diagnostics previously
@@ -91,7 +103,7 @@ static int mmc_set_mod_clk(struct sunxi_mmc_priv *priv, unsigned int hz)
 	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MACH_SUN8I_A83T) && priv->mmc_no != 2)
 		new_mode = false;
 
-	if (hz <= 24000000) {
+	if (hz <= 24000000 || sunxi_mmc_osc_only()) {
 		pll = CCM_MMC_CTRL_OSCM24;
 		pll_hz = 24000000;
 	} else {
